WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.440
One-fifth of the world's oil stays blocked in Hormuz until Washington meets Iran's terms. This is Omni View Top World News, episode 12. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:21.200
Iran's parliament speaker, Muhammad Bagger-Gullybaf, says the waterway stays shut until seven conditions in the Islamabad memorandum are met.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:27.060
Al Jazeera reports that North News quoted him saying, Washington sent some proposals through

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:32.540
a mediator after answering Tehran's plan. He says the time for wasting days and dictating

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:38.480
unilateral demands is over, and that Iran will both fight and negotiate. President Donald Trump

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.180
ruled out Tehran's reopening roadmap last week, hours after Iran offered it.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.180
Foreign Minister Abbas Aragji told diplomats in Tehran that Iran is serious about talks

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:53.860
and about defending itself, and that another American military move would meet a force

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:54.960
more ready than before.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.940
Spokesman Ismail Bugayi says Washington is still centered on nuclear talks, while getting

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.500
the straight open again is Tehran's main aim.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.960
Iraq, next door in the Middle East, has moved its own crewed past that same street for the

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:09.960
first time in decades.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:16.160
The national says director-general Ali Kais, told state media the Iraqi oil tankers company

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.800
shipped 2 million barrels on a very large crude carrier, taking some sales off-free on board

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:22.820
loading at Basra.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.900
Oil is at least 90% of Iraq's revenue, and before the war, most exports, about 3.3 million

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.660
barrels a day, left Basra and crossed the street.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.440
Oil Minister Basin Qudair said last month the country has been able to move 3 million barrels

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.040
a day since the start of September.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:45.320
The street has been effectively closed by Iran since the war broke out in February, with

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:50.880
missiles, drones, insurance spikes and naval clashes disrupting ships. In Ukraine,

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.600
a Russian drone hit Kiev's Pivnićni bridge on Sunday morning for a second day and injured two

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:02.820
people, as German Chancellor Friedrich Murts arrived without notice. The BBC reports Mayor Vitaly

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:07.600
Klitschko said the roadway was hit. He also said another drone damaged a heating main,

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.140
so the Desnionsky district in the northeast will be without hot water for a time.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:17.180
President Volodymyr Zelensky said a drone strike on a warehouse in Sumi killed

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:22.740
one person and a hit on a communication site in Denipro injured six. Ukraine's

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:28.660
Air Force said Russia sent 135 drones overnight, 52 of them jet-powered and that

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:33.680
125 projectiles were shot down. Russia's military said it will intensify

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.220
strikes and earlier said it hit two bridges used to move troops. The bridges

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.900
Stages are still standing, but the damage has jammed traffic in a capital of about 3 million,

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:49.220
and Germany, Ukraine's largest donor, has sent more than 43.3 billion euros, about

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.480
$48.8 billion, since the invasion began.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:58.640
In Ethiopia, federal troops and allied fighters were seen holding McKelle, the Tigray capital,

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.540
after taking the main regional airport, and the Tigray People's Liberation Front pulled

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.020
out, Al Jazeera reports.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:10.600
The Catholic Bishop said Thursday, the church grieves over fighting in Tigray, a far,

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.240
umhara, oromia, and other regions, and that war kills people and wrecks communities.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:22.200
They echoed Pope LEO, who on Wednesday said the guns are back in Tigray, a far and umhara,

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.560
and asked every party to choose dialogue.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:30.120
The Bishop said children, women, the elderly, and the sick bear the worst of it, and they

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.620
asked each side to treat another life as its own.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:38.460
In South Korea, President Lee Jae-myeong ordered a full investigation Sunday into personal

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:41.720
data leaks at banks, finance firms, and public agencies.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:48.380
Yeon-Hop reports Shin Han Bank said records on about 25,000 customers leaked, names, phone

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:53.440
numbers, and annual income among them, and sources said the hackers used advanced artificial

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.460
intelligence tools.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.620
Data on 89 Hana Bank customers leaked.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:03.800
Worry Bank and NH-Nonghiet Bank blocked the access and reported no leak, and KB Cookman

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.880
Bank was among those that reported attacks.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:10.980
Financial Services Commission Chairman Lee Oguen said nothing that could authorize a

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.700
payment appears to have leached so far.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:18.020
Warned the data could still feed voice phishing scams, and did not rule out artificial intelligence

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:18.760
in the attacks.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:24.000
The People Power Party said investigators should also look at possible North Korean involvement,

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:31.020
and attack traffic was reported from addresses in the United States, Japan, Singapore, Vietnam, and Britain.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:36.660
In Brazil, in South America, voting began Sunday between Lula and Flavio Bolsonaro,

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:42.080
with a runoff on October 25th if no one wins more than half, DW reports.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:48.560
In Gaza, an Israeli strike on a civilian vehicle killed one Palestinian and wounded at least 11.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.980
France 24 reports the military said it was targeting a Hamas militant.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:59.360
In Bosnia and Herzegovina, polls opened for about 3.4 million voters, and some stations

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.000
started late after new scanners failed, France 24 reports.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:09.260
In India, the deep water gas ceiling rose to $9.89 per million British thermal units,

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:14.960
from $8.90, while legacy-fueled gas stays capped at $7, rediff reports.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:21.920
In Egypt, subscriptions opened Sunday to a $19.2 million fund, about 1 billion Egyptian

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:27.900
pounds that will buy equity in distressed factories, deal room reports. On whether Ukraine should get

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:33.620
full European Union membership or an associated status with no vote, the case on both sides is

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:39.100
being laid out in Kiev today. Chancellor Friedrich Merz has said he doubts accession can happen in

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:44.700
the coming years. His offer would open the single market and give Ukraine observer status in the council,

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:50.480
the commission and the parliament, without a vote. His stated reason is that full entry will not come

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:55.500
soon, so associated status would open the market and the rooms now, still without a vote.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:06:00.440
He has refused Germany's tourist cruise missiles, a transfer he demanded in opposition.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:05.180
In his government has instead funded technical work on Ukraine's own long-range weapons,

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.340
Politico reports.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:12.200
President Zelensky has rejected that offer and said Ukraine needs full and equal membership

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:16.600
because the decisions that defend the country should not be made without Ukraine's vote.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:21.740
He described MERS as the leader of a country that consistently protects Ukrainian lives from

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:22.440
Russian strikes.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:26.860
Said the two sides are preparing decisions that would give Ukraine and Europe more

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:30.700
means to defend themselves, and said Russia must be stopped together.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.340
Both accept that MERS is in Kiev today.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:37.640
The next stated step is the agreements they say they are preparing on this visit.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:43.660
On Friday, foreign minister Johann Wadafull said Russia's leadership shows no real interest

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:46.140
in ending the war and means to continue it.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.160
Looking back over the past week,

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.740
three threads are worth catching if you miss them.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:54.820
Hurricane Polo, with winds near 115 miles an hour,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.640
near Baja, California, Sir,

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.760
